oney-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing on `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even`. `round_money` in `src/money.py` said it used banker's rounding (FIN-212), but it actually called `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n\nThis PR changes it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, so `2.665` now rounds to `2.66` as the test expects. `2.675` still rounds to `2.68`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR opened, but its reviewer list came back empty, so I'll request alex directly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01X4oq1vr2JmM7EdjqAG23tT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and the pull request against main is open with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py`'s comment said it used banker's rounding, but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So `2.665` rounded up to `2.67`, while `tests/test_money.py` expects `2.66`.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, as FIN-212 requires. This is commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). The PR came back with no reviewers listed even though I'd named alex when opening it, so I requested alex's review separately. alex is now listed as a reviewer.\n\nI didn't merge it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}